Water scarcity costs Africa an estimated $45 billion annually. In Sub-Saharan Africa, 400 million people lack basic drinking water. Agenda 2063 Aspiration 1 envisions an Africa with climate-resilient economies. You cannot have that without water intelligence.

PedPey Africa asked a simple question: What if we could predict water crises before they happen using AI?

1. THE AFRICAN WATER PARADOX

Africa has abundant water but poor water management. The problem is not lack of water, it is lack of visibility. Where is the water? When will it run out? Is it clean? Our governments were making decisions with 30-day-old data.

